# Selected ordinary CTF thermal histories — source proposal only

This immutable proposal adds a standalone thermal-history owner/API and eight
focused, unexecuted tests. It does not activate the runtime surface path, execute
EnergyPlus or Rust, initialize an environment, or establish SUR04/SUR07 gates.
Root owns any later application, formatting, testing and same-input observations.

The only existing-source change is one public module declaration after the
already applied, reviewed surface-binding module in the actual formatted parent.
No existing state, cache, initializer, coefficient math or surface consumer changes.
All new files, the exact parent before copy and three generated diffs are held.

## Exact bounded Original scope

Pinned EnergyPlus26.1 HeatBalanceSurfaceManager.cc2323–2357 and2381–2435 supply
the selected history suffix of InitThermalAndFluxHistories. The new initialization
function resets the four normal19-row histories to Native SurfInitialTemp23 and
positive-zero flux, optionally resets already allocated masters and counters,
then applies the selected actual outside boundary and public UValue in literal
term/surface order. Inside flux term1 reads outside flux term2 while it still has
its reset value; term2 is assigned later. This is intentionally not a uniform fill.

UpdateThermalHistories5245–5496 supplies the no-internal-source update. First-time
scratch allocation follows the actual flag, with exactly five zero-dimensioned
owners and then flag=false. Current flux uses actual SurfTempIn and actual CTF
constants. Source report signs and area multiplication are retained. This selected
mutation of four report arrays does not certify report initialization or completion.

The SimpleCTFOnly && !AnyConstrOverridesInModel branch moves/reuses the actual
last GLOBAL MaxCTFTerms+1 row, shifts all allocated surface columns, copies current
term1 to term2 and returns. It is not a per-construction vector truncation. Rows
above that global extent retain all supplied values/bits, including signed zeros
and NaN payloads. Source evaluation order across the four arrays is preserved.

The general branch captures the four block-start scratch values only when actual
CurrNumHist is zero. It increments the actual counter, assigns SumTime from that
counter and actual TimeStepZone, then performs the literal completed-master shift
or interpolation using actual NumHistories and CTFTimeStep. It does not infer a
counter, round a timestep ratio, reset scratch each visit, or interpolate masters.
NumCTFTerms==0 skips flux calculations but still reaches general counter handling.

## Actual owner contract

Callers supply already allocated fixed19 term-major normal buffers and their full
surface-ID layout, including columns outside the selected HT loops. Masters and
CurrNumHist remain optional actual allocations; scratch and FirstTimeFlag are
separate owners. No constructor/default creates an initialized environment.
Only the source first-time update branch allocates its five actual scratch arrays.

Selected surface rows borrow all12 public19 coefficient arrays/counts/dt/U, with
actual surface ID, current Construction ID and public-owner Construction ID.
They also supply actual algorithm/opaque/source selectors, boundary, resolved
SurfOutDryBulbTemp, area, SurfTempIn and inside/outside constants. SurfTempIn and
inside-temperature history term1 remain separate actual operands. No coefficient,
conductance, weather, surface solve, current temperature or history term is derived.

The caller supplies Zone/Space HT and opaque traversal groups and AllHTSurfaceList
in their true separate source orders. Membership/uniqueness and allocated shapes
are validated without sorting those traversals. This selected scope requires all
supplied HT rows to be ordinary opaque CTF/EMPD with no source and Outdoors or
Adiabatic boundaries. Extra allocated nonselected columns are retained and take
part in the literal global simple shift. Ground/window/other algorithm/internal
source paths are explicit unsupported scope, not approximated.

Actual global SimpleCTFOnly, EMS, construction-override, internal-source, MaxCTFTerms
and TimeStepZone are supplied independently. Initialization requires actual masters
when !SimpleCTFOnly || EMS. General update requires actual masters/counters. A false
first-time flag requires the actual allocated five scratch vectors. No missing
owner is reconstructed from numeric values. Caller-origin claims cannot be proved
retroactively by accepting two matching IDs; future lifecycle integration must own
the true binding/generation/context handoff and reject stale generations.

## Explicit representability limits

Negative or >=19 history term counts/global maxima cannot index this fixed owner.
An i32 counter without a representable successor is typed unavailable; it is not
saturated and no Native overflow/fatal outcome is claimed. There are no finite,
positive-dt, dt-ratio, R, area or convergence guards; supplied IEEE math is retained.

Simple MaxCTFTerms==0 would move Native current row1 itself before the later hard
copy. This interface explicitly declines that moved/unallocated-row state as
SimpleCurrentRowMove. It does not certify or repair that Native path. The pinned
all-resistive branch assigns NumCTFTerms=1 (Construction.cc990–993), and genuine
Init aggregate updates can propagate that count; no future model's global max or
selected gate is inferred from this source fact.

